==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|kné|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*knewą}}, originally from {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*ǵónu}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/kʰnjɛː/|lang=is}}
* {{rhymes|ɛː|lang=is}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|n|knés|kné}}

# {{context|archaic|or|poetic|lang=is}} a [[knee]]{{jump|is|knee|s}}

====Declension====
{{Icelandic declension hk sb 06 é|kn}}

====Synonyms====
* {{jump|s|is|knee}} {{l|is|hné}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|is|falla á kné}} (to [[genuflect]])
* {{l|is|ganga fyrir kné}} (to [[genuflect]])
* {{l|is|gera knéfall}} (to [[genuflect]])
* {{l|is|knéfall}}
* {{l|is|knéfiðla}}
* {{l|is|knékrjúpa}} (to [[genuflect]])
* {{l|is|knékrjúpa fyrir}} (to go down on one's knees for somebody)
* {{l|is|koma á kné}} (to defeat somebody)
* {{l|is|koma fyrir kné}} (to [[genuflect]])
* {{l|is|láta kné fylgja kviði}} (to let the knee follow the belly, to plant the knee on the belly; to [[ride roughshod over]], to show no mercy, to give no quarter)

